  data:  # 2c55
    kind: work_item  # 2c55
    title: "smart-test runs the full import-closure test set for a comment-only change: 814 test files (~17 min) for comment edits to 15 core modules"  # 2c55
    status: todo_soft  # 2c55
    priority: 3  # 2c55
    parent:  # 2c55
    tags:  # 2c55
    - smart_test  # 2c55
    - ci_infrastructure  # 2c55
    isbefore: []  # 2c55
    duplicate_of: []  # 2c55
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2c55
    pr_ref:  # 2c55
    description: "smart-test selects tests per changed FILE, so a change that touches only comments and docstrings runs the same import-closure test set as a code change.\n\nObserved: a comment-only change to 15 hypergumbo_core modules (taint.py, verify_claims.py, io_boundary.py, spec_validator.py, entrypoints.py, compact.py and 9 others; the ASTs, docstrings blanked, compare identical to HEAD) selected 968 dependent files and 814 test files, estimated ~17 min on 6 CPUs. No imported behaviour can change, so almost all of that run cannot fail.\n\nProposal: for each changed `.py` source file, parse HEAD's and the working tree's versions; if the ASTs are equal with docstrings blanked (`ast.dump` after replacing each module/class/function docstring constant with \"\"), treat the file as text-only and do NOT expand its import closure. Select for it only the tests that read its source as text.\n\nWhat must still run for a text-only file (the hazard; get this wrong and a gate rots green):\n- tests that read source text: the field-axis gate (`check-multi-value-field-axis-declaration` via test_multi_value_field_axis.py, which reads `# axis:` comments on ir.py / datamodels.py / io_boundary.py), docstring/comment-scanning checks, line-number and citation tests (WI-lujon: a test citing `bash.py:1353` by string), `# covers:` / `# pragma` parsers, check-docstring-drift's tests;\n- whole-tree gates the slice already misses (WI-nifif's shape) are no worse off, but must not get worse.\nFinding \"tests that read file X as text\" is the open design question: a static scan for the module's path or name as a string in tests (the WI-lujon mechanism, if it exists, may already be this), plus an explicit allowlist of whole-tree text gates. If that set cannot be built reliably, the fallback is to keep the current behaviour.\n\nAlso out of scope for the shortcut: a changed `# type:` comment or `# pragma: no cover` changes mypy or coverage results, though not the AST; `# pragma` lines must make a file NOT text-only (or coverage must still be measured for it). A changed `__doc__` read at runtime (e.g. spec_validator's verdict-enum check reads `ClaimVerdict.__doc__`) is a behaviour change, so docstring-only changes are text-only only for docstrings no code reads; simplest safe rule: blank comments only, keep docstrings in the comparison, unless a cheap check shows no `__doc__` reader.\n\nDone when: a comment-only change to a hub module selects only its text-reading tests (seconds, not minutes), the manifest written for CI reflects the same selection, and a test shows that a `# axis:` comment edit on io_boundary.py still selects the field-axis gate."  # 2c55
    fields: {}  # 2c55
- op: update  # 0f76
