  set:  # 0f76
    title: "smart-test: find the tests that read a source file as TEXT, and (owner sign-off) keep a comment-only change's import closure out of the CI manifest"  # 0f76
    description: "smart-test selects tests per changed FILE, so a change that touches only comments runs the same import-closure test set as a code change. Observed: a comment-only change to 15 hypergumbo_core modules (taint.py, verify_claims.py, io_boundary.py, spec_validator.py, entrypoints.py, compact.py and 9 others; ASTs identical to HEAD) selected 968 dependent files and 814 test files, ~17 min on 6 CPUs.\n\nSCOPE (adjusted): this item owns two things.\n\n(A) THE TEXT-READER SET, shared with the block-level narrowing item (this item isbefore it). For a source file X, the tests that read X as TEXT rather than executing it: the field-axis gate (test_multi_value_field_axis.py reads `# axis:` comments on ir.py / datamodels.py / io_boundary.py), citation and line-number tests (WI-lujon: a test citing `bash.py:1353` by string), docstring/comment-scanning checks, `# covers:` / `# pragma` parsers. Coverage cannot find these (they may execute nothing in X), so they need their own source: a static scan of tests for X's path or module name as a string (check whether WI-lujon's mechanism already is this), plus an explicit list of whole-tree text gates. If the set cannot be built reliably, nothing in this item ships.\n\n(B) THE CI-MANIFEST HALF. For a changed `.py` source file whose AST is identical to the base (comments only), do not expand its import closure into the manifest; select only its text-readers from (A). This is deterministic (an AST comparison, not the coverage index), but it NARROWS THE MERGE GATE, which the owner's 2026-08-16 option A on WI-kuliv / WI-bolot kept static: owner sign-off required before (B) lands.\nExceptions that keep the full closure: a changed `# pragma: no cover` or `# type:` comment (changes coverage or mypy without changing the AST); a docstring change (it is in the AST anyway, and spec_validator reads `ClaimVerdict.__doc__` at runtime).\n\nThe LOCAL half (a comment-only change runs seconds of tests locally) is now the block-level narrowing item: under a block-level keep set a comment-only edit changes no block, so it keeps only the text-readers from (A).\n\nDone when: (A) exists with a test that an `# axis:` comment edit on io_boundary.py selects the field-axis gate; and, if the owner approves (B), a comment-only change to a hub module writes a manifest of only its text-readers."  # 0f76
  add:  # 0f76
    isbefore: [WI-gapos-nubuz-vokod-jajul-magid-zajis-nakud-lomit]  # 0f76
